<h1 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px;">
    Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 5
</h1>
<p style="text-align: center; margin: 5px 0 15px 0;">
    <em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em>
</p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 67%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Traditional Style of Dress</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> She Is Wearing a Pollera.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: text: Interpret simple school notices.
concept: Link historical events to current events for class discussions.</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can interpret simple school notices about traditional dress by explaining their meaning to peers (e.g., reads a notice that says 'Traditional Dress Day is next Friday.' and explains, 'We need to wear a pollera or traditional clothes on Friday.').
Can link the historical use of traditional clothing to current celebrations by providing simple comparisons and using visuals (e.g., show pictures of a pollera and say, 'This pollera has an old-fashioned design and this pollera has a modern design.').
Can facilitate discussions on traditional clothing and modern clothing by asking basic questions (e.g., 'Who wears this?' and points to festival images).</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7; padding: 10px; border-radius: 8px;">
    The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages
</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows flashcards or realia of traditional Panamanian clothing (e.g., a small pollera, a tembleque). Students identify the clothing using familiar vocabulary. Teacher asks, 'What is this? Who wears this?' to activate prior knowledge about traditional clothing and celebrations.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models the pronunciation of key vocabulary for describing and explaining: /w/ in 'wearing', /t/ in 'traditional', and blends for /dr/ /ɛs/ in 'dress', /pr-ɪ-t-i/ in 'pretty'. The teacher uses simple sentences like, 'She is wearing a beautiful pollera. This dress is traditional.' and points to the visuals. Teacher demonstrates how to make a simple comparison: 'This pollera is old-fashioned. This one is modern.' using two different pictures.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is this a modern dress or a traditional dress?" (pointing to a pollera) - Expected answer: "Traditional dress."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Are we wearing this dress every day?" - Expected answer: "No." "When do we wear it?" - Expected answer: "At festivals / celebrations."</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[5-7 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Our Traditional Style of Dress".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A simple, illustrated school notice about a 'Traditional Dress Day' for an upcoming school event (e.g., "School Festival: Traditional Dress Day is next Friday, October 20th! Wear your best traditional clothing (pollera, montuno, etc.) to showcase our culture!"). The notice uses vocabulary like 'traditional clothing', 'celebration', 'event', 'showcase'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Interpreting simple school notices to understand instructions about cultural events. Describing traditional clothing and explaining its cultural significance.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> The teacher reads the notice aloud, then asks:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the notice about?" (Gist question) - Expected: "Traditional Dress Day."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is 'Traditional Dress Day' tomorrow?" (True/False) - Expected: "False. It's next Friday."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What can we wear on that day?" (Information matching) - Expected: "Pollera, montuno, traditional clothing."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[8-10 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Mediation.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Interpreting and explaining simple information about traditional clothing and events using present continuous, present simple, and WH-questions. Vocabulary: 'attire', 'celebration', 'event', 'traditional clothing', 'old-fashioned', 'modern', 'wear', 'explain'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Guided Explanation (Controlled Practice):</b> Students work individually or in pairs. The teacher provides sentence starters and the school notice. Students complete sentences to explain the notice in their own words (e.g., "The notice says we need to ________ on ________." "We are ________ traditional clothing."). They use the target grammar: 'We need to wear traditional clothing on Friday.'</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Compare and Contrast (Semi-controlled):</b> Teacher shows two pictures: one of an old-fashioned pollera and one of a modern version. Students use sentence frames to describe and compare: "This pollera is ________. It is ________. This pollera is ________. It is ________." (e.g., 'This pollera has an old-fashioned design.' 'This pollera has a modern design.' 'Women wear this at festivals now, and they wore it in the past too.').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Peer Notice Interpretation (Pair Interaction):</b> Students work in pairs. One student (Student A) briefly re-explains the school notice to their partner (Student B) using their own words. Student B then asks a simple WH-question (e.g., "What day is the event?", "Who wears the pollera?") for Student A to answer. They then swap roles. This activity practices explaining and asking basic questions to facilitate understanding.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[15-18 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Our Traditional Style of Dress".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Mini-Presentations of "Traditional Clothing Posters". Students, in small groups, present their previously created "Traditional Clothing Poster" (Project 1). They will take turns explaining elements of their poster and mediating information to their classmates.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group displays their poster showing traditional clothing.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">One student from the group starts by explaining a specific piece of clothing on the poster: "She is wearing a beautiful pollera." (Present Continuous)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Another student explains its cultural significance: "Women wear this dress for festivals and celebrations. It represents our community." (Present Simple, explaining cultural significance, using 'celebration', 'community', 'represent').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A third student links historical to current use or compares designs, using visuals: "Look at this picture; this design is old-fashioned. This one is modern. People use both for big events now." (linking historical/current, comparing, using 'old-fashioned', 'modern', 'event', 'use').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher encourages other students to ask simple WH-questions (e.g., "What is she wearing?", "When do they wear it?", "Who wears the jewelry?") to the presenting group. The presenting group mediates answers and facilitates the discussion.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[10-12 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist focusing on mediation skills and peer assessment of the poster explanations.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students present their "Traditional Clothing Poster" and explain its contents, interpreting the cultural significance and answering peer questions. Each student's ability to explain the meaning of their chosen traditional attire and relate it to celebrations will be assessed.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Clear pronunciation of /w/ in 'wearing', /t/ in 'traditional', and phonemic blends.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> (e.g., 'attire', 'celebration', 'traditional clothing', 'old-fashioned', 'modern', 'explain', 'showcase').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity of explanation:</b> Can clearly explain what the clothing is and when it is worn.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration and facilitation:</b> Asks/answers basic questions to peers.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar usage:</b> Uses present continuous ('She is wearing...') and present simple ('Women wear...') appropriately.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete the following sentences before leaving:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today, I learned how to explain _________."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new word I used today was _________."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[5-7 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student and Teacher Reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of explaining our traditional clothing was easy? What was difficult?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I help my friends understand our culture more?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in helping students mediate information about traditional clothing and the project? The poster presentations allowed for good integration of vocabulary and grammar. The peer questioning helped facilitate discussion.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments and scaffolds are needed for the next lesson or similar mediation tasks? Some students struggled to link historical events to current events; more explicit modeling and sentence starters could help. More practice with 'WH-questions' to facilitate discussions is also needed.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson concludes the theme "She Is Wearing a Pollera." The next unit will introduce a new theme related to daily routines and activities, building on the present simple and present continuous tenses. Students will continue to practice describing and explaining information in different contexts.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[2-3 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>